{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdxFQswmzcNKYRAAPMSF5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I don't have write access to files in this environment (no Edit/Write/Bash tool available), so I can't apply the fix directly. Here's what I found and the fix needed:\n\n**Root cause:** `src/queries/posts/post-list-query.ts:6` uses a static TanStack Query key — `[\"posts\"]` — that doesn't include the site slug:\n\n```ts\nexport function getPostListQueryOptions(siteSlug: string) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: [\"posts\"] as const,\n    queryFn: () => api.listPosts(siteSlug),\n  });\n}\n```\n\nBecause the key never changes when `siteSlug` changes, switching sites reuses site A's cached post list as the initial render for site B (TanStack Query shows cached data immediately, then refetches in the background) — that's the flash of the wrong site's posts before it \"corrects itself\" once the refetch for the new `siteSlug` resolves.\n\nThe fix is scoping the key by site, matching the pattern already used in `getPostQueryOptions` (`src/queries/posts/post-query.ts:6`, `[\"sites\", siteSlug, \"posts\", postId]`) — and matching the test that's already sitting there unfulfilled at `src/queries/posts/post-query-keys.test.ts:7`, which expects `[\"sites\", \"acme\", \"posts\"]`:\n\n```ts\nqueryKey: [\"sites\", siteSlug, \"posts\"] as const,\n```\n\nThat's a one-line change. Want me to walk you through applying it, or can you make the edit?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13522,"cache_read_input_tokens":37013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13522},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9777d602-410e-4f3f-b6e3-68ee8d000b06","uuid":"3d7aa13f-8f5e-46ec-b08f-3da